Subject: [PATCH] claude/skills/process-email: Prefix list commits with msg:
To: Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com>
Cc: lab-devel@p7x.dev
Change-Id: vnyzvxytwmuvtonvllnmtysqnmkrwqux

Commits on the mail bookmark carry messages, not changes to the mail
tooling, yet the skill named them with the mail: prefix that trunk
uses for the mail/ area. That made a posted message and a patch to
the mail scripts look alike in the log.

The list now marks message commits msg: <Subject>, as just
commit-mail on the mail bookmark already does, so the skill follows
the same form and its commits match everyone else's.
---
change-id: vnyzvxytwmuvtonvllnmtysqnmkrwqux

 .claude/skills/process-email/SKILL.md | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/.claude/skills/process-email/SKILL.md b/.claude/skills/process-email/SKILL.md
index ce0575e..8c1cfb2 100644
--- a/.claude/skills/process-email/SKILL.md
+++ b/.claude/skills/process-email/SKILL.md
@@ -216,7 +216,7 @@ and commit the series on its own:
     done
     cd ~/lab/mail.jj
     jj diff --summary      # only "A maildir/..." lines
-    jj commit -m "mail: Post [PATCH] <subject>"
+    jj commit -m "msg: <Subject of the first file>"
 
 ## 6. Reply
 
@@ -252,7 +252,7 @@ own:
     ~/lab/default.jj/libexec/mail/maildir-deliver.sh < /tmp/reply.eml
     cd ~/lab/mail.jj
     jj diff --summary      # only "A maildir/..." lines
-    jj commit -m "mail: Reply to <subject>"
+    jj commit -m "msg: <Subject of the reply>"
 
 ## 7. Push
 

